# Line endings: git stores every text file with LF and checks it out with LF on every platform,
# whatever core.autocrlf says, so a Windows checkout cannot introduce CRLF into the scripts the
# Linux server runs (a CRLF shebang line fails with "bad interpreter"). The mixed-line-ending
# pre-commit hook enforces the same rule on commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary media: never normalised, never text-diffed or merged. The PNG baselines under
# ci/reference/ are hashed byte for byte.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary

# Language-aware diff hunk headers (the enclosing fn/def/heading) in `git diff` and `git log -p`.
*.rs   diff=rust
*.py   diff=python
*.md   diff=markdown

# Written by cargo, never by hand: collapsed in GitHub diffs and left out of language statistics.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated=true
